## 1. Software source code — GNU AGPLv3, version 3 only

All software in this repository — `code/gftac/`, `tests/`, `conftest.py`,
`verify_book.py`, `verify_transcripts.py`, `build_pdf.py`,
`render_book_figures.py`, `.github/`, `tools/`, and the configuration files —
is licensed under the **GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only
(AGPL-3.0-only)**.

The complete, verbatim license text is included at
[`third_party/licenses/AGPL-3.0.txt`](third_party/licenses/AGPL-3.0.txt) and at
<https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt>.

Two consequences are stated here because they are easy to miss:

* **Remote network interaction is distribution.** If you modify the software
  and let users interact with it over a network, AGPL §13 requires you to offer
  those users the Corresponding Source of your modified version, at no charge.
* **Derivative works inherit the license.** AGPL §5(c) requires prominent
  modification notices and §10 forbids adding further restrictions. The patent
  grant in §11 is subject to the same terms.

The book's parity tests ship a trimmed, pinned copy of the companion SDKs under
`third_party/` so a fresh clone can verify itself. Those files keep their
upstream licenses; see §4 and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

